/*
================================================================================
TITLE            : Authentication Failure Summary by Source IP
FILE NAME        : authentication_anomalies.SPL
AUTHOR           : Serah Kathini Mulwa
TARGET INDEX     : cybersecurity_lab
SOURCETYPE       : _json
SOURCE DATASET   : normalised_events.jsonl (8 synthetic lab events)
STATUS           : Verified in Splunk Lab (All time on synthetic sample)
================================================================================

OBJECTIVE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Summarizes authentication failure events in the cybersecurity_lab index by
originating source.ip and sorts results from highest to lowest failure count.

WHAT THIS LAB OUTPUT SHOWS:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- In the Day 22 synthetic dataset (8 events total, 2 authentication_failure
  events), source.ip "192.0.2.25" shows failed_attempts = 2.
- A count of 2 in a small synthetic lab sample is an observed lab count, not
  proof of a confirmed attack on its own. Real SOC tuning requires higher
  thresholds, time-window context, and additional telemetry (such as account
  names, target hosts, and authentication logs).
================================================================================
*/

index=cybersecurity_lab sourcetype="_json" event.outcome="failure"
| stats count AS failed_attempts BY source.ip
| sort - failed_attempts
